{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1578844203,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI5NDEzMjExMjI="},"added":["external-tools"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1578844203,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI5NDEzMjExMjM="},"added":["feedback-desired"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1578870430,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MzQ2Nzg4OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4019#issuecomment-573467889"},"message":"the motivation was/is to not re-implement what was already implemented, and for many more archives than just .7z and .tar{,.xz,.gz}.  \nWe did have `.gz` and `.zip` at least as well.  I think I had some .rar and may be few others which I had \"handled\" with datalad at some point.\n\n\u003e I am thinking about reimplementing compress_file and decompress_file with direct calls to 7z and tar\n\nWell, I guess nobody would stop you... (or you could fix patool to benefit not only datalad but other users of patool as well).  If you are to reimplement - just make it configurable (to be able to force use of patool) and use patool for other types of archives support for which you wouldn't reimplement.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1578895916,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MzUyMTc5Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4019#issuecomment-573521792"},"message":"Point taken, but I am still not seeing the benefit of patool for our purposes. All of what you write above is possible with straight-up 7z cmdine alone. It supports all the formats you mentioned, including `tar.?` (so I wouldn't even bother with TAR). It might well be that the entire code to achieve the same results through 7z is less than the compatibility dance we are currently doing to pass information to patool.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1579097417,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI5NTA5MzI3MDQ="},"added":["conference agenda item"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1579098064,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3NDY4MDM3Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4019#issuecomment-574680373"},"message":"one of the issues I had with patool (and 7z for that matter) is handling large files: https://github.com/wummel/patool/issues/49","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1579102924,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50Mjk1MTI4NTUzMw=="},"added":[],"removed":["conference agenda item"]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1579105665,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3NDczOTE5NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4019#issuecomment-574739194"},"message":"I checked my recent work re archive file size. The largest archive I built has 1.9T, I can reliably extract arbitrary content from it:\n\n```\n$ ls -lh archive.7z\n-rw-r--r-- 1 me users 1.9T Nov 16 22:54 archive.7z\n$ 7z e archive.7z physio.json\n\n7-Zip (a) [64] 16.02 : Copyright (c) 1999-2016 Igor Pavlov : 2016-05-21\np7zip Version 16.02 (locale=en_US.UTF-8,Utf16=on,HugeFiles=on,64 bits,32 CPUs Intel(R) Xeon(R) Gold 6142 CPU @ 2.60GHz (50654),ASM,AES-NI)\n\nScanning the drive for archives:\n1 file, 2063868614059 bytes (1923 GiB)\n\nExtracting archive: archive.7z\n--\nPath = archive.7z\nType = 7z\nPhysical Size = 2063868614059\nHeaders Size = 391804\nMethod = Copy\nSolid = -\nBlocks = 42441\n\nEverything is Ok                                                         \n\nSize:       89\nCompressed: 2063868614059\n```\n\nThis particular archive uses no compression inside the container. I tested a 500G 7z with LZMA compression. It works equally fine.\n\n```\n$ 7z e archive2.7z IC_146_prob.png\n\n7-Zip (a) [64] 16.02 : Copyright (c) 1999-2016 Igor Pavlov : 2016-05-21\np7zip Version 16.02 (locale=en_US.UTF-8,Utf16=on,HugeFiles=on,64 bits,32 CPUs Intel(R) Xeon(R) Gold 6142 CPU @ 2.60GHz (50654),ASM,AES-NI)\n\nScanning the drive for archives:\n1 file, 527731712730 bytes (492 GiB)\n\nExtracting archive: archive2.7z\n--\nPath = archive2.7z\nType = 7z\nPhysical Size = 527731712730\nHeaders Size = 6660694\nMethod = LZMA2:24 BCJ\nSolid = +\nBlocks = 587\n\nEverything is Ok                                                             \n\nFiles: 725\nSize:       1604829618\nCompressed: 527731712730\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1579110087,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3NDc3MjIwOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4019#issuecomment-574772208"},"message":"The references issue was extracting from already existing .zip files, not .7z","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1579110087,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDMzODM1OTkwMQ=="},"target":"837294bc5961c762a17237b2f756ee1363033914c811470b0fce1d8f7e86ae91","message":"The referenced issue was extracting from already existing .zip files, not .7z","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1579110207,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3NDc3MzA2Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4019#issuecomment-574773063"},"message":"Anyway, implementing alternative handling of archives is ok with me, even making it to be default, but then falling to patool via config or automatically if eg unknown format or simply 7z is not available","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestam